Bill Of Materials
-Arduino Nano
-(opt.) terminal socket for Nano mcu
-pir sensor
-3 jumper wires
-Arduino IDE
-Ubuntu(Linux) OS
-Jazzy(ROS2 Distro)

Create the Module
-connect signal wire to pinD2
-connect + to mcu VCC
-connect - to mcu GND
-verify module with '01_PIR_module.jpeg'

Upload the sketch
-upload the sketch titled '02_PIR_sketch' to the mcu using the Arduino IDE

Test the Sketch
-Verify that the module and sketch are working properly.
-proper operation should show valid data in the serial display

Create Entry Node
-in the ROS2 project create an entry node for the mcu/pir module
-the entry node is titled '03_PIR_entryNode'
-add entry node to setup.py 'entry-points'

BSR(Build/Source/Run)
-navigate to the workspace and build the project (colcon build)
-source the project (source install/setup.bash)
-run the node (ros2 run <project name> <node name>

Verify the results
-test the sensors ability to detect motion and transmit serial data to the droid brain
-open a new terminal and use 'ros2 topic echo <topic name>
-success should appear as serial data printing to terminal
